ed as American " [:a {:href "/athletes/51236"} "Amy White"] " challenged the leaders, and she hung on to win gold in 2:12.38, with White taking silver and Pătrăşcoiu the bronze. White had been 1983 Pan American champion in this event when she was only 14-years-old. De Rover’s time made her the eighth fastest performer of all-time. Pătrăşcoiu won the first-ever Olympic swimming medal for Romania."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "135"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/49319"} "Jolanda de Rover"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "2:13.50 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:12.38 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "265"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51236"} "Amy White"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:15.40 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:13.04 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "213"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/49946"} "Anca Pătrășcoiu"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} "2:16.71 (2 h4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:13.29 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "16"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45108"